### Schedule Api Tests - Integrated Enemy Management
### Enemies are now managed directly via POST and PUT /schedules endpoints

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
### Update with actual userId from database
@userId = ea74963f-9c54-449c-b925-7508d2b96ece
@scheduleId = 7bb24d4b-c9b5-44fd-8ce1-8f8ecf559ffe

### ===== STEP 1: GET EXISTING USER_ID =====
### Run this query to see what userIds exist in database
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Accept: application/json

### Copy ID of one user and replace @userId above

### ===== STEP 2: CREATE SCHEDULES =====

### CREATE Schedule without enemies
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "name": "Daily Farm Schedule",
  "world": "pl218",
  "scheduleType": "Main"
}

### CREATE Schedule with enemies (provide their TribalWars IDs)
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "name": "Reconnaissance Mission",
  "world": "pl218",
  "scheduleType": "Reconnaissance",
  "enemyTribalWarsIds": [189, 197]
}

### CREATE Schedule with single enemy
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "name": "Fake Attack Training",
  "world": "pl220",
  "scheduleType": "Fake",
  "enemyTribalWarsIds": [189]
}

### ===== STEP 3: FETCHING SCHEDULES =====

### GET all schedules for user (includes enemyIds list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

### GET schedule by ID (includes enemyIds list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{userId}}/{{scheduleId}}
Accept: application/json

### ===== STEP 4: GET TRIBES FOR WORLD =====
### Fetch list of tribes/enemies for schedule's world (cached for 15 minutes)
### Use the TribalWarsIds from response to set enemies
GET {{baseUrl}}/worlds/pl218/tribes
Accept: application/json

### ===== STEP 5: UPDATE SCHEDULE WITH ENEMIES =====

### UPDATE schedule and set enemies (replace entire enemy list)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Daily Farm Schedule",
  "world": "pl218",
  "scheduleType": "Main",
  "enemyTribalWarsIds": [189, 197, 205, 210]
}

### UPDATE schedule and clear enemies (empty list)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Farm Schedule",
  "world": "pl218",
  "scheduleType": "Main",
  "enemyTribalWarsIds": []
}

### UPDATE schedule without changing enemies (omit enemyTribalWarsIds)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Renamed Schedule",
  "world": "pl218",
  "scheduleType": "Main"
}

### ===== STEP 6: DELETE SCHEDULE =====

### DELETE schedule (also deletes associated enemies)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{scheduleId}}

### ===== INSTRUCTIONS =====
### 1. Run GET /users - get list of existing users
### 2. Copy user ID and replace @userId
### 3. (Optional) Get tribes: GET /worlds/{world}/tribes
### 4. Create schedule with or without enemies via POST /schedules
### 5. Copy returned schedule ID and replace @scheduleId
### 6. GET schedule to verify (response includes enemyIds)
### 7. Update schedule enemies via PUT /schedules/{scheduleId}
###    - If enemyTribalWarsIds is provided, it replaces the entire list
###    - If enemyTribalWarsIds is omitted, enemies are NOT changed
###    - Empty array [] clears all enemies
### 8. Delete schedule when done

### Response Format:
### ScheduleDto includes:
### - id, userId, name, creationDate, world, scheduleType
### - enemyIds: List<int> - TribalWars IDs of enemy tribes (empty if none)

### Available World values: pl218, pl219, pl220, pl221, pl222, pl223
### Available ScheduleType values: Fake, Reconnaissance, Main
### Note: All provided enemyTribalWarsIds must exist in the selected world
